cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Pharmakon or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Pharmakon: an uncertainty-aware, 2,000-year map of Greek and Byzantine pharmacology"
abstract: >-
  Pharmakon reads Dioscorides' De materia medica in Greek, gives a probability for the modern species behind each
  ancient plant name, traces every use through Galen, John the Physician and modern Greek villages, runs a
  leakage-free temporal backtest, and ranks untested plant–condition research leads with toxicity and conservation
  flags. Research hypotheses only, not medical advice.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Arpit
    affiliation: "National Institute of Technology Hamirpur"
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LSUDOKO/Pharmakon"
url: "https://pharmakon.adoranto737.workers.dev"
keywords:
